81
00:05:10.945 --> 00:05:15.383
Oh four: an object I D that isn't
a service principal in the tenant.

82
00:05:15.383 --> 00:05:18.344
Oh five is the licensing
record and the rings.

83
00:05:18.344 --> 00:05:23.082
Oh six: an out-of-scope identity recorded
without the control that covers it.

84
00:05:23.082 --> 00:05:27.010
Oh seven: a policy that isn't
report-only and block-only,

85
00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:30.133
for all resources and
all client app types.

86
00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:33.807
Oh eight keeps the egress
ranges narrow and untrusted.

87
00:05:33.807 --> 00:05:35.745
And oh nine guards enforcement.

88
00:05:35.745 --> 00:05:39.400
A finding exits with code
one and fails the pipeline.

89
00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.175
Unit 3 begins with the plan.

90
00:05:45.175 --> 00:05:50.113
It compares the files with the tenant
and gives each policy one of six actions.

91
00:05:50.113 --> 00:05:52.951
Create, when the policy
isn't in the tenant,

92
00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:57.876
and a new policy is always created
report-only, whatever its ring's state.

93
00:05:57.876 --> 00:06:02.650
Update, when it differs; the patch
carries only the properties that changed.

94
00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.700
No change, when it matches.

95
00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.607
Blocked, for a location policy whose named

96
00:06:07.607 --> 00:06:11.012
location doesn't exist yet;
the next run creates it.

97
00:06:11.012 --> 00:06:15.776
Held, when the ring is marked for
enforcement but this run may not enforce it.

98
00:06:15.776 --> 00:06:19.748
And not in repository, for a
workload policy that no file names,

99
00:06:19.748 --> 00:06:22.163
such as one someone made in the portal.

100
00:06:22.163 --> 00:06:24.100
It's reported and left alone.

101
00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.963
The code has no delete at all.

102
00:06:25.963 --> 00:06:30.068
Rollback drops the ring from the
enforcement record and applies,

103
00:06:30.068 --> 00:06:32.790
so its policies go back to report-only.

104
00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:40.146
Turning a policy on is the moment
